From: Xios Project <xios@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Keep WebKitGTK on Unix IPC attachments on Darwin

The GTK port uses Unix-domain-socket IPC even when cross-built for Darwin.
OS(DARWIN) alone selected MachSendRight, whose implementation is only available
to Cocoa ports, leaving std::optional<Attachment> with an incomplete type.
Limit Mach-port attachments to Cocoa and let GTK use UnixFileDescriptor.

--- a/Source/WebKit/Platform/IPC/Attachment.h
+++ b/Source/WebKit/Platform/IPC/Attachment.h
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@
 
 #pragma once
 
-#if OS(DARWIN)
+#if PLATFORM(COCOA)
 #include <wtf/MachSendRight.h>
 #endif
 
@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@ namespace IPC {
 
 // IPC::Attachment is a type representing objects that cannot be transferred as data,
 // rather they are transferred via operating system cross-process communication primitives.
-#if OS(DARWIN)
+#if PLATFORM(COCOA)
 using Attachment = MachSendRight;
 #elif OS(WINDOWS)
 struct Attachment { }; // Windows does not need attachments at the moment.
